title: Trade Union Law
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/tuc.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and union_law_timer <= 0
on-arrival: union_law_timer = 6; month_actions += 1

= Trade Union Law

The Employment Secretary, [+ employment_secretary +], comes to discuss the unions. [? if union_power >= 60 : The union barons still believe they can bring down any government that crosses them. ?][? if union_power < 60 and union_power > 40 : The balance of power in industry is shifting. ?][? if union_power <= 40 : The unions are weaker than they have been for a generation. ?]

- @cautious_act: Introduce a cautious Employment Bill.
- @tough_act: Introduce a bill to strip the unions of their legal immunities.
- @trade_union_bill: Introduce a bill for secret ballots before strikes.
- @ballots: Pay for secret ballots.
- @tuc: Invite the TUC to talks.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@cautious_act
view-if: employment_acts = 0 and bill_employment1 = 0 and bill_employment2 = 0 and time >= bill_employment1_wait
subtitle: Restricts secondary picketing and the closed shop, step by step. Law in about five months, if Parliament agrees.
choose-if: bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ bill_room_text +]
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 3 if employment_dry = 0; bill_new = "employment1"
call: bill_introduce

[+ employment_secretary +] publishes the Employment Bill. It limits picketing to a worker's own place of work and gives some protection against the closed shop. The TUC protests, but nobody talks of a general strike.

@tough_act
view-if: bill_employment2 = 0 and (bill_employment1 = 0 or bill_employment1 = 6) and time >= bill_employment2_wait
subtitle: Makes unions liable for damages from unlawful strikes. Requires a dry Employment Secretary. Law in about five months.
choose-if: employment_dry = 1 and bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if employment_dry = 0 : [+ employment_secretary +] will not bring forward a bill this radical. ?][? if employment_dry = 1 : [+ bill_room_text +] ?]
on-arrival: dry_dissent -= 5; wet_dissent += 6; bill_new = "employment2"
call: bill_introduce

The bill will take away the unions' blanket immunity from being sued. A union that calls an unlawful strike will put its funds at risk. Union leaders are already comparing it to the law passed after the General Strike.

@trade_union_bill
view-if: employment_acts >= 1 and bill_trade_union = 0 and time >= bill_trade_union_wait
subtitle: No ballot, no immunity. Law in about five months.
choose-if: bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [+ bill_room_text +]
on-arrival: dry_dissent -= 2; right_dissent -= 1; wet_dissent += 1; bill_new = "trade_union"
call: bill_introduce

The Trade Union Bill will make every strike, every union executive and every political fund answer to a secret ballot of the members. The union leaders say it is none of the government's business how a union runs itself.

@ballots
subtitle: -1 budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; union_power -= 5; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent)

Public money pays for postal ballots on strikes and union elections. Moderates start to win union elections.

@tuc
on-arrival: union_power += 5; strike_wave -= 1; wet_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent += 4

Union leaders come to Downing Street for beer and sandwiches. It's the first time since 1979, and the dries hope it's the last.
